---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy | SoloKit" description="How SoloKit handles your data: the tools run in your browser and what you type is not uploaded.">
  <div class="wrap page">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="faint">Last updated 13 October 2026</p>

    <h2>The short version</h2>
    <p>SoloKit's tools run in your browser. The names, numbers, addresses and documents you type are not sent to us or to anyone else, and there are no accounts.</p>

    <h2>What is stored on your device</h2>
    <p>To remember your work, SoloKit saves the following in your browser's local storage on this device:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your business details and logo, if you add them;</li>
      <li>invoices and quotes you create;</li>
      <li>time tracker entries;</li>
      <li>your last inputs in the calculators and planner, and your light or dark theme choice.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>This data never leaves your device unless you download a backup and share it yourself. You can delete it all from <a href={`${base}workspace/#data`}>Workspace → Backup and data</a>, or by clearing your browser's site data.</p>

    <h2>Offline use</h2>
    <p>SoloKit uses a service worker to keep a copy of its pages on your device, so the tools work without an internet connection. It stores only the website's own files.</p>

    <h2>Exchange rates</h2>
    <p>If you choose a local currency in the payment fee calculator, your browser requests today's exchange rates from open.er-api.com. That request contains only the currency code. Like any website, that service can see your IP address.</p>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>The site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub may record technical information, such as your IP address, when your browser requests a page, to keep the service secure and running. See GitHub's privacy statement for details.</p>

    <h2>Analytics and advertising</h2>
    <p>SoloKit does not currently use analytics or advertising cookies. If that changes, for example to show ads that keep the tools free, this policy will be updated first, naming the providers used (such as Google) and how to opt out of personalised ads.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about privacy: <a href="mailto:saifsiddiqui1717@gmail.com">saifsiddiqui1717@gmail.com</a>.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
